### Frontend: WebSocket Client

#### File: [dashboard/js/dashboard.js](file:///c:/Users/TalentBridgeDubai/Documents/app-web-dev/trx/dashboard/js/dashboard.js)

**Complete rewrite** from polling to WebSocket-based system.

**Key Changes**:

**1. WebSocket Connection**:
```javascript
connectWebSocket() {
  this.ws = new WebSocket('ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws');
  
  this.ws.onopen = () => {
    console.log('WebSocket connected');
    this.updateConnectionStatus(true);
  };
  
  this.ws.onmessage = (event) => {
    const signals = JSON.parse(event.data);
    this.handleSignalUpdate(signals);
  };
  
  this.ws.onclose = () => {
    this.attemptReconnect();
  };
}
```

**2. Auto-Reconnection Logic**:
```javascript
attemptReconnect() {
  if (this.reconnectAttempts >= this.maxReconnectAttempts) {
    this.updateStatusText('Connection failed - please refresh');
    return;
  }
  
  this.reconnectAttempts++;
  setTimeout(() => {
    this.connectWebSocket();
  }, this.reconnectDelay); // 3 seconds
}
```

**Features**:
- Max 5 reconnection attempts
- 3-second delay between attempts
- Status updates during reconnection
- User feedback on failure

**3. Signal Update Handler**:
```javascript
handleSignalUpdate(signals) {
  const container = document.getElementById('signals-grid');
  container.innerHTML = '';
  
  for (const [instrument, signal] of Object.entries(signals)) {
    const cardHTML = createSignalCard(instrument, signal);
    container.innerHTML += cardHTML;
  }
  
  this.initializeGauges(signals);
  this.updateLastUpdateTime();
}
```

**4. Removed Polling**:
- ❌ Deleted `setInterval()` refresh
- ❌ Deleted `refreshInterval` property
- ❌ Deleted countdown timer logic
- ❌ Deleted `loadSignals()` HTTP polling

**5. Updated Controls**:
- **Refresh button**: Now reconnects WebSocket
- **Pause button**: Hidden (WebSocket is always-on)

